. *** PART 3. IS EACH TREATMENT AS GOOD AS RANDOMLY ASSIGNED? (BALANCE TESTS) ***
. * T2 (siblings) and T3 (classes) each put all waves in one table; simulation figures follow.
. 
. ** 3.1 Sibling gender (2014 and 2022) **
. * If sibling gender were random: (a) about 51.2% of babies are boys, so the average
. * number of brothers should be about 0.512 times the number of siblings; (b) it should
. * not depend on the student's own sex or on family characteristics.
. eststo clear

. foreach w in 2014 2022 {
  2.     di _n "---- Sibling gender, wave `w' ----"
  3.     forvalues n = 1/4 {
  4.         quietly summ brothers if s_sib & wave == `w' & nsib == `n'
  5.         di "Families with `n' sibling(s): N = " r(N) ", mean brothers = " %5.3f r(mean) ", expected = " %5.3f `n'*0.512
  6.     }
  7.     cap drop one_sib_bro
  8.     gen byte one_sib_bro = (brothers > 0) if s_sib & wave == `w' & nsib == 1
  9.     di "Share of one-sibling families with a brother, tested against 0.512:"
 10.     prtest one_sib_bro == 0.512
 11.     drop one_sib_bro
 12. 
.     * Does the share of brothers predict other (predetermined) characteristics?
.     foreach x in girl fas_z momwork dadwork {
 13.         eststo B`w'_`x': quietly reg `x' share_bro i.age_grp i.nsib if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
 14.     }
 15.     if `w' == 2014 {
 16.         foreach x in mfses mmses {
 17.             eststo B`w'_`x': quietly reg `x' share_bro i.age_grp i.nsib if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
 18.         }
 19.     }
 20.     di "Joint test: do own sex, affluence and parents' work predict the share of brothers?"
 21.     quietly reg share_bro girl fas_z momwork dadwork i.age_grp i.nsib if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
 22.     testparm girl fas_z momwork dadwork
 23. }

