. *** PART 4. HEADLINE RESULTS ***
. * Effects are in standard deviations of the outcome. Standard errors are clustered by class.
. * For each wave and outcome we run three models:
. *   (1) minimal controls   (2) HEADLINE specification   (3) HEADLINE + school-by-age-group FE
. eststo clear

. 
. ** 4.1 The models, wave by wave **
. foreach w in 2014 2022 {
  2.     foreach y in complaints3 lifesat_z {
  3.         eststo m1s_`y'_`w': quietly reg `y' share_bro $SIB_MIN if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
  4.         eststo m2s_`y'_`w': quietly reg `y' share_bro $SIB if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
  5.         if "`y'" == "complaints3" di "Wave `w', siblings: smallest effect we could reliably detect (80% power), all sister
> s -> all brothers: " %5.3f 2.8*_se[share_bro]
  6.         eststo m3s_`y'_`w': quietly areg `y' share_bro girl i.nsib fas_z $EMP if s_sib & wave == `w', ///
>             absorb(school_age) vce(cluster classid)
  7.     }
  8. }
