. ** A8. Ordered probit **
. * Ordinary regression treats answers such as "never ... every day" as equally spaced numbers.
. * Ordered probit only uses their order. If both agree, the equal-spacing assumption is not
. * driving the results. It needs whole-number answers, so it is run on the three symptom
. * questions one at a time and on life satisfaction (not on the averaged index).
. foreach w in 2014 2022 {
  2.     eststo clear
  3.     foreach y in rev_feellow rev_irritable rev_nervous lifesat {
  4.         eststo ols_`y': quietly reg `y' share_bro $SIB if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
  5.         eststo oprobit_`y': quietly oprobit `y' share_bro $SIB if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
  6.     }
  7.     esttab ols_* oprobit_* using "$out/tables/A8_oprobit_siblings_`w'.tex", replace `tex' keep(share_bro) ///
>         title("Sibling gender: OLS and ordered probit, `w'")
  8.     quietly oprobit rev_feellow share_bro $SIB if s_sib & wave == `w', vce(cluster classid)
  9.     di "Wave `w': change in the probability of feeling low EVERY DAY, all sisters -> all brothers:"
 10.     margins, dydx(share_bro) predict(outcome(5))
 11. }
